        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p104
        `licence route` "(כה)2" (LIST "teaching hearing-impaired pupils") `grades 7 to 12`
            (LIST `a degree` 1 (LIST "hearing impairment (another Israeli institution)") `Israel only`,
                  `completion exams` (LIST `principles of special education`),
                  `a positive supervision report`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p105
        `licence route` "(כה)3" (LIST "teaching hearing-impaired pupils") `grades 7 to 12`
            (LIST `a degree` 1 (LIST "hearing impairment") `abroad`,
                  `completion exams` (LIST `principles of special education`),
                  `completion exams` `the Hebrew exams`,
                  `a positive supervision report`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p106 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p107
        `licence route` "(כו)1" (LIST "communication disorders", "occupational therapy", "physiotherapy", "art therapy") `grades 7 to 12`
            (LIST `a degree` 1 (LIST "the subject applied for") `Israel only`,
                  `completion exams` (LIST `principles of special education`),
                  `a positive supervision report`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p108
        `licence route` "(כו)2" (LIST "communication disorders", "occupational therapy", "physiotherapy", "art therapy") `grades 7 to 12`
            (LIST `a degree` 1 (LIST "the subject applied for") `abroad`,
                  `completion exams` (LIST `principles of special education`),
                  `completion exams` `the Hebrew exams`,
                  `a positive supervision report`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p109 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p110
        `licence route` "(כז)1" (LIST "seamanship") `the junior high school`
            (LIST `a teaching certificate` (LIST "physical education") `Israel only` `post-primary or junior high`,
                  `a further condition` "finished the maritime track"),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p111
        `licence route` "(כז)2" (LIST "seamanship") `the junior high school`
            (LIST `a further condition` "a sailing-coach certificate of the Wingate Institute coaches' school",
                  `a matriculation certificate`,
                  `completion exams` `the pedagogical exams`, `a positive supervision report`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p112
        `licence route` "(כז)3" (LIST "seamanship") `the junior high school`
            (LIST `a further condition` "an IDF naval officer with a skipper's certificate, of the rank of captain or above",
                  `a matriculation certificate`,
                  `completion exams` `the pedagogical exams`, `a positive supervision report`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p113
        `licence route` "(כז)4" (LIST "seamanship") `the junior high school`
            (LIST `a further condition` "an IDF sailor's certificate",
                  `a matriculation certificate`,
                  `completion exams` `the pedagogical exams`, `a positive supervision report`)

-- F-1.21-b: the Bible's junior-high licence is given "by section ב' above,
-- except subsection (ג)". 1.21.2.2 numbers its paragraphs 1 to 4 and has no
-- section ב'; read as its second paragraph, that paragraph licenses grades
-- 7-12, not the junior high school, and its (ג) is an Israeli route, not the
-- foreign one the clause means to leave out. The junior-high paragraph is 4,
-- whose (ג) is the foreign route — as every other subject's rule says.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p58
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade range`
DECIDE `the grades of the general route named` n IS
    map (GIVEN q YIELD q's `licence grades`) (filter (GIVEN q YIELD q's `route name` EQUALS n) `the general routes`)

`"section ב', except (ג)" does not name the junior-high rules` MEANS
        `the grades of the general route named` "2(ג)" EQUALS LIST `grades 7 to 12`
    AND `the grades of the general route named` "4(ג)" EQUALS LIST `the junior high school`
    AND NOT any (GIVEN q YIELD q's `route name` EQUALS "ב(ג)") `the general routes`
#ASSERT `"section ב', except (ג)" does not name the junior-high rules`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p114 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p115 A note pointing elsewhere: licences for the maritime track of the upper division are given by special circular ט' (5756), the technological regulations of 1.21.3.

-- (יז)'s notes: (א) studies abroad are examined on their merits and handled
-- as an exception by the grading department after consulting the chief
-- supervisor; (ב) sends to (לח) for the Haredi sector.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p69 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p70
GIVEN `country of the studies` IS A `country of study`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Oral-Law application is handled as an exception` `country of the studies` IF
    NOT `country of the studies` EQUALS `Israel`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p71 A pointer to (לח) below for licences in the Haredi sector, encoded there.

-- (יח) ¶73: one licence covers general history and the history of the
-- Jewish people. A degree in one part qualifies if it included four courses
-- of the other part, from different periods, of 2 weekly hours or more each
-- (or they were completed at a university or by exams); that condition is
-- for teachers without an Israeli history teaching certificate — one who has
-- that certificate qualifies on a degree in one part.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p73
GIVEN `degree in one part only` IS A BOOLEAN, `courses of the other part, 2 weekly hours or more, from different periods` IS A NUMBER, `has an Israeli history teaching certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the degree counts as a degree in history` `degree in one part only` `courses of the other part, 2 weekly hours or more, from different periods` `has an Israeli history teaching certificate` IF
       NOT `degree in one part only`
    OR `has an Israeli history teaching certificate`
    OR `courses of the other part, 2 weekly hours or more, from different periods` AT LEAST 4

#ASSERT `the degree counts as a degree in history` TRUE 4 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the degree counts as a degree in history` TRUE 3 FALSE

-- (כד)1: the 350 completion hours are 194 in the summer course, 44 of first
-- aid and two 56-hour field campuses — the text's own sum.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p98
`the Shelach completion hours` MEANS 194 PLUS 44 PLUS 2 TIMES 56
#ASSERT `the Shelach completion hours` EQUALS 350

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p116 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p117 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_3/p118 The subsection's source list (אסמכתא): two Director-General's circulars.

§§ `1.21.2.4 רשיונות הוראה קבועים למקצועות מיוחדים (חלק ב)`

-- ¶1–¶3: in this subsection "a degree from an English-speaking country"
-- means studies held in that country, the employee living there for all the
-- years of study; so degrees of a foreign university's branch studied in
-- Israel do not qualify.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p1 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p3
GIVEN `studied in that country` IS A BOOLEAN, `lived there all the years of study` IS A BOOLEAN, `a branch studied in Israel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a degree from an English-speaking country` `studied in that country` `lived there all the years of study` `a branch studied in Israel` IF
    `studied in that country` AND `lived there all the years of study` AND NOT `a branch studied in Israel`

#ASSERT NOT `a degree from an English-speaking country` FALSE FALSE TRUE

