`the special-subject routes` MEANS
    concat (LIST `the special-subject routes, part א`, `the special-subject routes, part ב`)

-- (לח) 1–3: the Haredi Oral-Law licence asks these exams; ¶196: one who
-- passes them all and has a positive opinion on the practical work gets a
-- licence for metivtot and junior yeshivot — 7–10 on an equivalent first
-- degree, 7–12 on a second or third.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p187
`the Haredi Oral-Law exams` MEANS
    LIST
        `300 pages of Gemara`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p190
        `introduction to the Oral Law`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p191 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p192
        `educational thought`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p193
        `ways of teaching and the Bible cantillation`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p194
        `learning processes`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p195
        `ways of teaching the Oral Law`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p124 Heading: "notes" (to the English routes).

-- English note 3 (¶127): wherever "linguistics" is written, English
-- linguistics is meant.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p127
GIVEN field IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `what "linguistics" means in the English routes` field IS
    IF field EQUALS "linguistics" THEN "English linguistics" ELSE field

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p202 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p203 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p204 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p205 The subsection's source list (אסמכתא): three Director-General's circulars.

§§ `1.21.2.5 רשיונות הוראה קבועים למקצועות חריגים`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p1 Heading: "6. exceptional licences".

-- (א): a degree in one subject and a teaching certificate in another, from a
-- recognised higher-education or teacher-training institution (for junior
-- high or post-primary), entitle to a permanent licence in the other
-- subject. F-1.21-d: the clause sets no grades. Read by the general rule of
-- 1.21.2.2 — a first degree for grades 7–10, a second for 7–12.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p2
`the exceptional routes` MEANS
    LIST
        `licence route` "1.21.2.5(א) first degree" (LIST "any subject") `grades 7 to 10`
            (LIST `a degree` 1 (LIST "any subject") `Israel or abroad`,
                  `a teaching certificate` (LIST "the subject applied for") `Israel or abroad` `post-primary or junior high`),
        `licence route` "1.21.2.5(א) second degree" (LIST "any subject") `grades 7 to 12`
            (LIST `a degree` 2 (LIST "any subject") `Israel or abroad`,
                  `a teaching certificate` (LIST "the subject applied for") `Israel or abroad` `post-primary or junior high`)

-- F-1.21-d: (א) as printed names a subject and no grades, where every other
-- permanent route names its grades. For a first-degree holder with a
-- post-primary certificate, the general rule gives grades 7–10 and the
-- certificate's level would give 7–12.
DECLARE `exceptional clause as printed` HAS
    `clause letter`        IS A STRING
    `grades it names`      IS A MAYBE `grade range`

`clause (א) as printed` MEANS `exceptional clause as printed` "(א)" NOTHING

`1.21.2.5(א) states no grades of its own` MEANS
        `clause (א) as printed`'s `grades it names` EQUALS NOTHING
    AND map (GIVEN q YIELD q's `licence grades`)
            (filter (GIVEN q YIELD q's `route name` EQUALS "1.21.2.5(א) first degree") `the exceptional routes`)
        EQUALS LIST `grades 7 to 10`
#ASSERT `1.21.2.5(א) states no grades of its own`

-- (ב): a degree in applied mathematics, physics or chemistry counts — for
-- professional education — toward one more subject.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p3
DECLARE `extra subject` HAS
    `degree in`        IS A STRING
    `also counts for`  IS A STRING

`the extra subjects` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p4
        `extra subject` "applied mathematics" "physics",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p5
        `extra subject` "physics" "mathematics",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p6
        `extra subject` "chemistry" "physics"

GIVEN `field of the degree` IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the subjects the degree's professional education covers` `field of the degree` IS
    `field of the degree` FOLLOWED BY
        map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `also counts for`)
            (filter (GIVEN x YIELD x's `degree in` EQUALS `field of the degree`) `the extra subjects`)

#ASSERT `the subjects the degree's professional education covers` "chemistry" EQUALS LIST "chemistry", "physics"

-- (ג): a double-major graduate with a teaching certificate in one major
-- only gets a permanent licence in the other too, (1) if the other is in the
-- same group as the licensed one, or (2) if the table pairs them — the
-- table is not in the corpus text (¶14 is its label), so (2) is an input.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p7 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p8 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p9 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p12 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p13
DECLARE `subject group` HAS
    `group name`     IS A STRING
    `group subjects` IS A LIST OF STRING

`the subject groups` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p10
        `subject group` "א" (LIST "history", "geography", "social sciences", "political science", "civics", "philosophy"),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p11
        `subject group` "ב" (LIST "physics", "chemistry", "biology", "agriculture")

GIVEN `licensed major` IS A STRING, `other major` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in one group` `licensed major` `other major` IF
    any (GIVEN g YIELD elem `licensed major` (g's `group subjects`) AND elem `other major` (g's `group subjects`)) `the subject groups`

GIVEN `licensed major` IS A STRING, `other major` IS A STRING, `the table pairs them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other major is licensed too` `licensed major` `other major` `the table pairs them` IF
    `in one group` `licensed major` `other major` OR `the table pairs them`

#ASSERT `the other major is licensed too` "history" "civics" FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the other major is licensed too` "history" "physics" FALSE

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p14 The label of the table of paired subjects; the table is not in the corpus text.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p15 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_5/p16 The subsection's source list (אסמכתא).

§§ `1.21.2.6 רשיונות הוראה זמניים`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6/p1 Heading: "chapter ג': temporary teaching licences".

DECLARE `temporary-licence applicant` HAS
    `recommended by the principal and the supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `level of a degree in the subject`          IS A NUMBER  @desc 0 for none, 1 first, 2 second or higher; some subjects divide the grades otherwise, as their permanent routes say
    `level of an equivalent grade in an arts, sport or Oral-Law subject` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 for none; the subjects are painting and art, music, physical education, dance, theatre and the Oral Law
    `a regular third-year student of the relevant major` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Shelach applicant with an Israeli degree in a listed major and a certified Shelach instructor's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a third-year student of teacher training toward a junior-high certificate in the subject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a seamanship applicant with a Wingate coach, IDF sailor or naval officer certificate` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ¶2: a temporary licence to teach a subject needs the recommendation of the
-- principal and of the school's supervisor, and ONE of the conditions below;
-- each condition gives the grades it licenses.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6/p2
GIVEN a IS A `temporary-licence applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade range`
DECIDE `the grades a temporary licence may cover` a IS
    IF NOT a's `recommended by the principal and the supervisor`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE concat (LIST
        (`grades on a degree in the subject` a),
        (`grades on an equivalent grade` a),
        (`grades as a third-year student of the major` a),
        (`grades for Shelach` a),
        (`grades as a third-year student of teacher training` a),
        (`grades for seamanship` a))

-- A degree in the subject: a first degree licenses grades 7–10, a second or
-- higher 7–12.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_1__para_1
GIVEN a IS A `temporary-licence applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade range`
DECIDE `grades on a degree in the subject` a IS
    IF a's `level of a degree in the subject` AT LEAST 2 THEN LIST `grades 7 to 12`
    ELSE IF a's `level of a degree in the subject` AT LEAST 1 THEN LIST `grades 7 to 10` ELSE EMPTY

-- An equivalent academic grade in painting and art, music, physical
-- education, dance, theatre or the Oral Law: equivalent to a first degree,
-- grades 7–10; to a second or higher, 7–12.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_1__para_2
GIVEN a IS A `temporary-licence applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade range`
DECIDE `grades on an equivalent grade` a IS
    IF a's `level of an equivalent grade in an arts, sport or Oral-Law subject` AT LEAST 2 THEN LIST `grades 7 to 12`
    ELSE IF a's `level of an equivalent grade in an arts, sport or Oral-Law subject` AT LEAST 1 THEN LIST `grades 7 to 10` ELSE EMPTY

-- A regular third-year student of the relevant major: grades 7–10.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_1__para_3
GIVEN a IS A `temporary-licence applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade range`
DECIDE `grades as a third-year student of the major` a IS
    IF a's `a regular third-year student of the relevant major` THEN LIST `grades 7 to 10` ELSE EMPTY

-- Shelach: an Israeli degree in history, geography, archaeology or Land of
-- Israel studies and a certified Shelach instructor's certificate: 7–12.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_1__para_4
GIVEN a IS A `temporary-licence applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade range`
DECIDE `grades for Shelach` a IS
    IF a's `a Shelach applicant with an Israeli degree in a listed major and a certified Shelach instructor's certificate` THEN LIST `grades 7 to 12` ELSE EMPTY

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_1__para_4/p2 Heading: "for the junior high school".

-- For the junior high school: a third-year student of an Israeli
-- teacher-training institution, toward a junior-high certificate in the subject.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_2__para_1
GIVEN a IS A `temporary-licence applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade range`
DECIDE `grades as a third-year student of teacher training` a IS
    IF a's `a third-year student of teacher training toward a junior-high certificate in the subject` THEN LIST `the junior high school` ELSE EMPTY

-- For the junior high school: seamanship, on a Wingate sailing-coach, IDF
-- sailor or naval officer certificate.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_2__para_2
GIVEN a IS A `temporary-licence applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `grade range`
DECIDE `grades for seamanship` a IS
    IF a's `a seamanship applicant with a Wingate coach, IDF sailor or naval officer certificate` THEN LIST `the junior high school` ELSE EMPTY

-- ¶2 of the seamanship clause: a temporary licence is given for the first
-- two working years (one year in exceptional cases), for the subject, school
-- and grades written in it; ¶3: it may be extended to a third year, and in
-- the most exceptional cases a special approval allows a fourth. Years are
-- counted from the first year of work.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_2__para_2/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6__hc_2__para_2/p3
GIVEN `year of work` IS A NUMBER, `an exceptional one-year licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `extended to a third year` IS A BOOLEAN, `special approval for a fourth year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the temporary licence covers the year` `year of work` `an exceptional one-year licence` `extended to a third year` `special approval for a fourth year` IF
    BRANCH IF `year of work` AT MOST 1 THEN TRUE
           IF `year of work` EQUALS 2  THEN NOT `an exceptional one-year licence`
           IF `year of work` EQUALS 3  THEN `extended to a third year`
           IF `year of work` EQUALS 4  THEN `extended to a third year` AND `special approval for a fourth year`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

`a recommended BA holder` MEANS `temporary-licence applicant` WITH
    `recommended by the principal and the supervisor` IS TRUE
    `level of a degree in the subject`                IS 1
    `level of an equivalent grade in an arts, sport or Oral-Law subject` IS 0
    `a regular third-year student of the relevant major` IS FALSE
    `a Shelach applicant with an Israeli degree in a listed major and a certified Shelach instructor's certificate` IS FALSE
    `a third-year student of teacher training toward a junior-high certificate in the subject` IS FALSE
    `a seamanship applicant with a Wingate coach, IDF sailor or naval officer certificate` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the grades a temporary licence may cover` `a recommended BA holder` EQUALS LIST `grades 7 to 10`
#ASSERT NOT `the temporary licence covers the year` 4 FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_6/p4 The subsection's source list (אסמכתא).

§§ `1.21.2.7 בחינות השלמה ופטור מבחינות אלו`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p1 Heading: "chapter ד': completion exams".

-- 1 (¶2): an employee with full professional training in a subject (as in
-- 1.21.2.2–1.21.2.6), aged 25 or more, lacking pedagogical and/or Hebrew
-- education, in the second year of teaching that subject in an Israeli
-- post-primary school (junior high included), with a positive report that
-- year from a supervisor of the Ministry or of Labour and Welfare, may get a
-- permit to sit completion exams for a permanent licence.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p2
GIVEN `full professional training` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, `lacks pedagogical or Hebrew education` IS A BOOLEAN, `year teaching the subject in an Israeli post-primary school` IS A NUMBER, `positive report that year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may get a permit to sit completion exams` `full professional training` age `lacks pedagogical or Hebrew education` `year teaching the subject in an Israeli post-primary school` `positive report that year` IF
        `full professional training`
    AND age AT LEAST 25
    AND `lacks pedagogical or Hebrew education`
    AND `year teaching the subject in an Israeli post-primary school` EQUALS 2
    AND `positive report that year`

#ASSERT `may get a permit to sit completion exams` TRUE 30 TRUE 2 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `may get a permit to sit completion exams` TRUE 24 TRUE 2 TRUE

-- ¶3–¶7: the pedagogical exams.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p3
`the pedagogical exams` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p4
        `adolescent psychology`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p5
        `theory of education`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p6
        `theory of teaching`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p7
        `methodology of teaching the subject`

-- ¶8–¶14: the Hebrew exams.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p8
`the Hebrew exams` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p9
        `Hebrew language`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p10
        `Bible`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p11
        `Hebrew literature`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p12
        `Jewish history`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p13
        `civics`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p14
        `Jewish heritage`

-- ¶15: teachers in the Arab and Druze sector sit Hebrew language only.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p15
GIVEN `teaches in the Arab or Druze sector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `exam`
DECIDE `the Hebrew exams to sit` `teaches in the Arab or Druze sector` IS
    IF `teaches in the Arab or Druze sector`
    THEN LIST `Hebrew language`
    ELSE `the Hebrew exams`

-- 2 (¶16): further exams by the subject's chief supervisor, for example:
-- (א) ¶17 an English or French teacher without an Israeli teaching
-- certificate sits the methodology of teaching the language in every case;
-- (ב) ¶18–¶21 an English teacher sits also English proficiency (80 or more),
-- English and American literature and pedagogical English linguistics;
-- (ג) ¶23–¶25 an Oral-Law teacher with an equivalent grade sits 300 pages of
-- Gemara and an introduction to the Oral Law.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p16 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p17 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p18 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p19 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p20 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p21 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p23 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p24 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p25
GIVEN `the subject` IS A STRING, `has an Israeli teaching certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `on an equivalent grade` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `exam`
DECIDE `the further exams for the subject` `the subject` `has an Israeli teaching certificate` `on an equivalent grade` IS
    concat (LIST
        (IF (`the subject` EQUALS "English" OR `the subject` EQUALS "French") AND NOT `has an Israeli teaching certificate`
         THEN LIST `methodology of teaching the subject` ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF `the subject` EQUALS "English"
         THEN LIST `English proficiency, mark 80 or more`, `English and American literature`, `pedagogical linguistics`
         ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF `the subject` EQUALS "the Oral Law" AND `on an equivalent grade`
         THEN LIST `300 pages of Gemara`, `introduction to the Oral Law`
         ELSE EMPTY))

#ASSERT `the further exams for the subject` "French" FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `methodology of teaching the subject`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p22 A pointer to the English exam lists of 1.21.2.4(כח), encoded there.

-- 3 (¶26): a holder of a permanent licence who finished a major in another
-- subject at a recognised institution, outside the licensed subject's group
-- (1.21.2.5(ג)), sits the methodology of teaching the other subject.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p26
GIVEN `licensed subject` IS A STRING, `other subject` IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF `exam`
DECIDE `the exams for the other major` `licensed subject` `other subject` IS
    IF `in one group` `licensed subject` `other subject`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE LIST `methodology of teaching the subject`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p27 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p28 Headings: "chapter ה': exemption from completion exams" and "1. general".

-- 1 (¶29): one examined, with a positive mark, in a final external or
-- internal exam of a Hebrew or pedagogical subject of 2 weekly hours or more
-- at a recognised Israeli institution — or in a pedagogical subject at a
-- recognised institution abroad — is exempt from that exam. It is the
-- `passed` holding of the exam itself.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p29
GIVEN `weekly hours of the course` IS A NUMBER, `positive mark` IS A BOOLEAN, `recognised institution in Israel` IS A BOOLEAN, `a pedagogical subject at a recognised institution abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an institution's exam counts as passed` `weekly hours of the course` `positive mark` `recognised institution in Israel` `a pedagogical subject at a recognised institution abroad` IF
        `weekly hours of the course` AT LEAST 2
    AND `positive mark`
    AND (`recognised institution in Israel` OR `a pedagogical subject at a recognised institution abroad`)

DECLARE `exemption` HAS
    `exemption ground of the row` IS AN `exemption ground`
    `exemption subjects`          IS A LIST OF STRING
    `exams exempted`              IS A LIST OF `exam`

-- The exemptions of chapter ה' 2–4 (and the English notes of 1.21.2.4, and
-- the Oral-Law exemptions of 1.21.2.4(לח) and 2(ג) above), as printed.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p30
`the exemptions` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p31
        `exemption` `finished an English-medium high school` (LIST "English") (LIST `English proficiency, mark 80 or more`, `pedagogical linguistics`),
        `exemption` `a degree or teaching certificate from an English-speaking country` (LIST "English") (LIST `English proficiency, mark 80 or more`, `pedagogical linguistics`),
        `exemption` `an Israeli degree in English and an Israeli English teaching certificate` (LIST "English") (LIST `English proficiency, mark 80 or more`, `pedagogical linguistics`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p32 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p126
        `exemption` `a degree in English literature` (LIST "English") (LIST `English and American literature`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p33 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p125
        `exemption` `a TESOL degree or diploma, or a degree in English or applied linguistics or English language` (LIST "English") (LIST `pedagogical linguistics`),
        `exemption` `an Israeli English teaching certificate` (LIST "English") (LIST `pedagogical linguistics`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p34
        `exemption` `an Israeli English teaching certificate` (LIST "English") (LIST `methodology of teaching the subject`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p35 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p36
        `exemption` `a degree in education, applying for the pedagogical subjects` (LIST "the pedagogical subjects") (LIST `theory of education`, `methodology of teaching the subject`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p37
        `exemption` `a degree in psychology or Ben-Gurion behavioural sciences` (LIST "any subject") (LIST `adolescent psychology`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p38
        `exemption` `the same, applying for a psychology licence` (LIST "psychology") (LIST `adolescent psychology`, `methodology of teaching the subject`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p39
        `exemption` `a primary teaching certificate, or a reserve-exams certification` (LIST "any subject") (LIST `theory of education`, `theory of teaching`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p40
        `exemption` `a certified professional instructor of the government technological institute` (LIST "any subject") (LIST `adolescent psychology`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p41
        `exemption` `a double major with education, applying for the other major` (LIST "any subject") (LIST `adolescent psychology`, `theory of education`, `theory of teaching`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p42
        `exemption` `an associate professor, docent or senior lecturer teaching the subject` (LIST "any subject") `the pedagogical exams`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p43
        `exemption` `a permanent post-primary principal for three years or more` (LIST "any subject") `the pedagogical exams`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p44
        `exemption` `a pedagogical instructor, mentor or methodology lecturer for two years or more` (LIST "any subject") (LIST `methodology of teaching the subject`, `theory of teaching`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p45
        `exemption` `taught the subject eight consecutive years, the last four in the same post-primary school` (LIST "any subject") (LIST `methodology of teaching the subject`),
        -- (יא) as adopted (F-1.21-c): a pre-State teacher in a post-primary
        -- school is exempt from every exam; in a primary school, from the
        -- pedagogical exams except adolescent psychology.
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p46
        `exemption` `taught in a Hebrew post-primary school before the State` (LIST "any subject") (concat (LIST `the pedagogical exams`, `the Hebrew exams`)),
        `exemption` `taught in a Hebrew primary school before the State` (LIST "any subject") (LIST `theory of education`, `theory of teaching`, `methodology of teaching the subject`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p47
        `exemption` `a certified kindergarten teacher` (LIST "any subject") (LIST `theory of education`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p48 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p49
        `exemption` `taught in a Hebrew primary school before the State` (LIST "any subject") `the Hebrew exams`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p50
        `exemption` `began teaching in Israel by 5721 and teaches continuously` (LIST "any subject") `the Hebrew exams`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p51
        `exemption` `holds a "Jerusalem certificate"` (LIST "any subject") `the Hebrew exams`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p52
        `exemption` `a foreign-language, vocational or science teacher over 50 with sufficient Hebrew in the supervisor's view` (LIST "English", "French", "a foreign language", "a vocational subject", "a natural science") `the Hebrew exams`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p53
        `exemption` `a foreign-language, science or vocational teacher certified in Israel as a teacher for the diaspora, with sufficient Hebrew` (LIST "English", "French", "a foreign language", "a vocational subject", "a natural science") `the Hebrew exams`,
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p188 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p24
        `exemption` `a rabbinical higher-education certificate of the Chief Rabbinate` (LIST "the Oral Law", "the Oral Law in the Haredi sector") (LIST `300 pages of Gemara`),
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_4/p189
        `exemption` `an equivalent grade to a second or third degree in the Oral Law` (LIST "the Oral Law", "the Oral Law in the Haredi sector") (LIST `300 pages of Gemara`)

-- F-1.21-c: (יא) as printed first exempts every pre-State teacher from the
-- pedagogical exams, then requires one who taught in a primary school to
-- sit adolescent psychology — one of the pedagogical exams.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p46
`(יא)'s first sentence exempts from` MEANS `the pedagogical exams`
`(יא)'s last sentence requires of a primary teacher` MEANS LIST `adolescent psychology`

`the pre-State primary teacher is exempt from and required to sit adolescent psychology` MEANS
    any (GIVEN e YIELD elem e `(יא)'s first sentence exempts from`) `(יא)'s last sentence requires of a primary teacher`
#ASSERT `the pre-State primary teacher is exempt from and required to sit adolescent psychology`

§§ `1.21.2.7 An exam passed or exempted`

-- An exam counts as sat when it was passed or when a ground the applicant
-- holds exempts from it for the subject (the table above).
GIVEN hs IS A LIST OF `holding`
      `the subject` IS A STRING
      e IS AN `exam`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has passed or is exempt from` hs `the subject` e IF
       elem (`passed` e) hs
    OR any (GIVEN x YIELD elem (`has the ground` (x's `exemption ground of the row`)) hs
                      AND `the field matches` (x's `exemption subjects`) `the subject` `the subject`
                      AND elem e (x's `exams exempted`))
           `the exemptions`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p54 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p55 The subsection's source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_2_7/p56 The heading of 1.21.3, "a teaching licence for a technological subject", printed at the end of this subsection.

§§ `1.21.3 רשיון הוראה למקצוע טכנולוגי`

-- 1 (¶1): every teaching employee of a post-primary institution needs a
-- licence from the Ministry, and the principal answers for no one teaching
-- but by it — besides the employment approval of circular נד/9 (1.21.4).
-- The rule is 1.21.2.1's, `may teach in a post-primary school`.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p1
GIVEN `licensed for the track's subject and grade` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the employment approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may teach a technological subject` `licensed for the track's subject and grade` `has the employment approval` IF
    `may teach in a post-primary school` `licensed for the track's subject and grade` `has the employment approval`

-- 2 (¶2): these regulations apply to grades 10 to 12; junior-high
-- regulations will be published separately.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p2
GIVEN grade IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the technological regulations apply to the grade` grade IF
    grade AT LEAST 10 AND grade AT MOST 12

-- 3 (¶3): the regulations apply "from ו' באלול התשנ"ה (1 January 1996)";
-- the 1982 regulations are cancelled, except for one who began training
-- "before the end of the school year", who may be licensed under them.
-- F-1.21-a: by the Hebrew calendar ו' באלול התשנ"ה is 1 September 1995
-- (and 1 January 1996 is ט' בטבת התשנ"ו): the clause names two dates four
-- months apart.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p3
`the Hebrew date given, in the civil calendar` MEANS 19950901
`the civil date given` MEANS 19960101

`the effective date is printed as two different days` MEANS
    NOT `the Hebrew date given, in the civil calendar` EQUALS `the civil date given`
#ASSERT `the effective date is printed as two different days`

DECLARE `technological regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the regulations of 1.21.3`
    `the regulations of 1982`

-- The reading adopted (F-1.21-a): the civil date, 1.1.1996, as the date the
-- clause spells out; the transition keeps the 1982 regulations for one who
-- began training before it.
GIVEN `date training began` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `technological regulations`
DECIDE `the regulations that govern the licence` `date training began` IS
    IF `date training began` LESS THAN `the civil date given`
    THEN `the regulations of 1982`
    ELSE `the regulations of 1.21.3`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p4 Paragraph 4 places these regulations within the takanon, for teaching employees of the technological track; it adds no rule.

-- 5 (¶5): the subjects are classed by the character of their content
-- (theoretical or practical) and by the grades (10, 11, 12) they are taught in.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p5
DECLARE `character of content` IS ONE OF
    `theoretical`
    `practical`

-- 8 (¶8): the levels of professional and pedagogical education. The legend
-- itself is not in the corpus text; its marks are levels 1 to 3 (level 1 is
-- a practical engineer — ¶14; 2 and 3 are academic) and level א (a senior
-- certified teacher — ¶15).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p8
DECLARE `education level` IS ONE OF
    `level 1`
    `level 2`
    `level 3`
    `level א`

-- 9א (¶10): levels 1–3 are in ascending order; level א stands alone, outside
-- that order. 9ג (¶12): the levels are the minimum for teaching a subject.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p10 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p12
GIVEN l IS AN `education level`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rank on the ladder` l IS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `level 1` THEN 1
    WHEN `level 2` THEN 2
    WHEN `level 3` THEN 3
    WHEN `level א` THEN 0

GIVEN `level held` IS AN `education level`, `levels named` IS A LIST OF `education level`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the level qualifies` `level held` `levels named` IF
       elem `level held` `levels named`
    OR (    `rank on the ladder` `level held` GREATER THAN 0
        AND any (GIVEN l YIELD `rank on the ladder` l GREATER THAN 0 AND `rank on the ladder` l AT MOST `rank on the ladder` `level held`) `levels named`)

-- 9ב (¶11): every level and degree is in the field of the subject or the
-- track taught.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p11
GIVEN `field of the education` IS A STRING, `subject or track` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the education is in the field` `field of the education` `subject or track` IF
    `field of the education` EQUALS `subject or track`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p13 Heading: "examples".

-- The text's examples. ¶14: a practical engineer of machines (level 1) may
-- teach "chapters of mechanics" (10.01) in grade 10 only; an academic (levels
-- 2–3) in grades 10–12. ¶15: a mark "1,א" lets both level 1 and level א teach
-- a subject.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p14 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p15
DECLARE `subject entry` HAS
    `subject code`   IS A STRING
    `subject name`   IS A STRING
    `entry grade`    IS A NUMBER
    `levels listed`  IS A LIST OF `education level`

`chapters of mechanics, as the example gives it` MEANS
    LIST `subject entry` "10.01" "chapters of mechanics" 10 (LIST `level 1`),
         `subject entry` "10.01" "chapters of mechanics" 11 (LIST `level 2`),
         `subject entry` "10.01" "chapters of mechanics" 12 (LIST `level 2`)

GIVEN `level held` IS AN `education level`, code IS A STRING, grade IS A NUMBER, entries IS A LIST OF `subject entry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may teach the subject in the grade` `level held` code grade entries IF
    any (GIVEN x YIELD x's `subject code` EQUALS code AND x's `entry grade` EQUALS grade AND `the level qualifies` `level held` (x's `levels listed`))
        entries

#ASSERT `may teach the subject in the grade` `level 1` "10.01" 10 `chapters of mechanics, as the example gives it`
#ASSERT NOT `may teach the subject in the grade` `level 1` "10.01" 11 `chapters of mechanics, as the example gives it`
#ASSERT `may teach the subject in the grade` `level 3` "10.01" 12 `chapters of mechanics, as the example gives it`
#ASSERT `the level qualifies` `level א` (LIST `level 1`, `level א`)
#ASSERT NOT `the level qualifies` `level א` (LIST `level 1`)

-- 6 (¶6): the licence is by track; the principal places the teacher in the
-- subjects and grades written in the licence's annex. 14 (¶37): the
-- requirements of each track follow,
-- marked by the legend's levels. 10ד (¶21): the licence carries the annex of
-- subjects and grades.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p37 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p21
GIVEN `level held` IS AN `education level`
      `annex of the licence` IS A LIST OF `subject entry`
      code IS A STRING
      grade IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal may place the teacher` `level held` `annex of the licence` code grade IF
        `the technological regulations apply to the grade` grade
    AND `may teach the subject in the grade` `level held` code grade `annex of the licence`

-- 7 (¶7): a permanent licence in a track, when the education level meets
-- one of the legend's items (8) and the teacher is fit for the subjects by
-- this circular's requirements.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p7
GIVEN `level held` IS AN `education level`
      `levels the legend admits` IS A LIST OF `education level`
      `fit for the subjects by the circular's requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to a permanent licence in the track` `level held` `levels the legend admits` `fit for the subjects by the circular's requirements` IF
        `the level qualifies` `level held` `levels the legend admits`
    AND `fit for the subjects by the circular's requirements`

-- 8's note (¶9): a foreign degree holder completes Hebrew education in Bible,
-- Hebrew language, literature, history and civics.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p9
GIVEN `degree from abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `exam`
DECIDE `the Hebrew education a technological teacher completes` `degree from abroad` IS
    IF `degree from abroad`
    THEN LIST `Bible`, `Hebrew language`, `Hebrew literature`, `Jewish history`, `civics`
    ELSE EMPTY

-- 10 (¶16–¶20): the application is made on form ח"ת 050.218, filled by the
-- employee (part א) and signed by the principal (ב) and the track's central
-- supervisor (ג), who writes the subject codes and an opinion on the
-- teacher's work; the national supervisor of training fills part ד for an
-- additional licence under 11. It goes, with the documents, to the grading
-- department; a licence issues to one entitled, given a positive opinion of
-- the central supervisor.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p16 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p17 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p18 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p19 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p20
DECLARE `technological application` HAS
    `on form 050.218`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `part א filled by the employee`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `part ב signed by the principal`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `part ג signed by the central supervisor, with codes and opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for an additional licence`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `part ד filled by the national supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `documents attached`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the central supervisor's opinion is positive` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN a IS A `technological application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is complete` a IF
        a's `on form 050.218`
    AND a's `part א filled by the employee`
    AND a's `part ב signed by the principal`
    AND a's `part ג signed by the central supervisor, with codes and opinion`
    AND a's `documents attached`
    AND ((NOT a's `for an additional licence`) OR a's `part ד filled by the national supervisor`)

GIVEN a IS A `technological application`, `entitled under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a technological licence issues` a `entitled under the regulations` IF
    `the application is complete` a AND `entitled under the regulations` AND a's `the central supervisor's opinion is positive`

-- 11 (¶22): a holder of a permanent licence under these regulations is
-- entitled to an additional licence if ALL of: ¶23 trained in further
-- subjects as the science-and-technology division sets; ¶24 passed every
-- task of the training; ¶25 recommended by the track's chief supervisor and
-- the national supervisor of training.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p22 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p23 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p24 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p25
GIVEN `holds a permanent licence under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN, `trained in further subjects` IS A BOOLEAN, `passed every task` IS A BOOLEAN, `recommended by both supervisors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to an additional technological licence` `holds a permanent licence under the regulations` `trained in further subjects` `passed every task` `recommended by both supervisors` IF
    `holds a permanent licence under the regulations` AND `trained in further subjects` AND `passed every task` AND `recommended by both supervisors`

-- 12 (¶26): a temporary licence for one who meets ONE of: ¶27 full
-- professional education (levels 1–3) without the pedagogical; ¶28 a
-- regular third-year student of technological teacher training; ¶29 a
-- regular third-year (or later) student of a recognised higher-education
-- institution in the field. ¶30–¶31: it lasts up to two years, for the
-- school, track, subjects and grades written in it; it may be extended to a
-- third year, and in special cases one more.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p26 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p27 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p28 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p29
GIVEN `full professional education without the pedagogical` IS A BOOLEAN, `third-year student of technological teacher training` IS A BOOLEAN, `third-year or later student in the field` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to a temporary technological licence` `full professional education without the pedagogical` `third-year student of technological teacher training` `third-year or later student in the field` IF
    `full professional education without the pedagogical` OR `third-year student of technological teacher training` OR `third-year or later student in the field`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p30 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p31
GIVEN `year of the licence` IS A NUMBER, `extended to a third year` IS A BOOLEAN, `extended again in a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the temporary technological licence covers the year` `year of the licence` `extended to a third year` `extended again in a special case` IF
    BRANCH IF `year of the licence` AT MOST 2 THEN TRUE
           IF `year of the licence` EQUALS 3  THEN `extended to a third year`
           IF `year of the licence` EQUALS 4  THEN `extended to a third year` AND `extended again in a special case`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 13 (¶32): a permit to sit the pedagogical exams (theory of education,
-- theory of teaching, adolescent psychology, methodology of the track's
-- subjects) and the Hebrew ones of the legend, for one who meets ALL of:
-- ¶33 full professional education (a degree or practical engineer) and no
-- pedagogical education; ¶34 aged 25 or more; ¶35 in the second year of
-- teaching technological subjects in a post-primary school; ¶36 a positive
-- report of the professional supervision from a lesson in the last year.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p32 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p33 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p34 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p35 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p36
GIVEN `full professional education without the pedagogical` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, `year teaching technological subjects` IS A NUMBER, `positive report from a lesson last year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may get a technological exam permit` `full professional education without the pedagogical` age `year teaching technological subjects` `positive report from a lesson last year` IF
        `full professional education without the pedagogical`
    AND age AT LEAST 25
    AND `year teaching technological subjects` EQUALS 2
    AND `positive report from a lesson last year`

#ASSERT `may get a technological exam permit` TRUE 26 2 TRUE

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p38 The track and subject codes are those of the 1991 timetable booklet for the technological track, as updated to 31.8.94; the codes are data, no rule.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p39 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p40 The subsection's source list (אסמכתא): special circular ט' (5756).

-- 1.21.3.2–1.21.3.19 (¶41): the tracks, each with its code. Their tables of
-- subjects are not in the corpus text; the tracks are.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p41
DECLARE `technological track` HAS
    `track code` IS A NUMBER
    `track name` IS A STRING

`the technological tracks` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p42
        `technological track` 10 "machines",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p43
        `technological track` 11 "electricity and electronics",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p44
        `technological track` 12 "building and architecture",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p45
        `technological track` 13 "woodwork",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p46
        `technological track` 14 "information technologies",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p47
        `technological track` 15 "industrial chemistry",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p48
        `technological track` 16 "biotechnology",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_1/p49
        `technological track` 17 "administration",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_10
        `technological track` 18 "industry and management",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11
        `technological track` 19 "tourism",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p1
        `technological track` 20 "design arts",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p2
        `technological track` 21 "communication technologies",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p3
        `technological track` 22 "fashion",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p4
        `technological track` 23 "beauty care",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p5
        `technological track` 24 "nursing and paramedical professions",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p6
        `technological track` 25 "education (of infants)",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p7
        `technological track` 26 "maritime education",
        @ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p8
        `technological track` 30 "science and technology"

GIVEN code IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a track of the regulations` code IF
    any (GIVEN t YIELD t's `track code` EQUALS code) `the technological tracks`

#ASSERT `a track of the regulations` 26
#ASSERT NOT `a track of the regulations` 27

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p9 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p10 Headings "annexes" and "a specimen of technological teaching licences"; the specimen is not in the corpus text.

§§ `1.21.4 אישור העסקה`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p11 The heading of 1.21.4, "employment approval".

-- 1 (¶12): by section 16A of the Supervision of Schools Law 1969, no one
-- employs an education worker unless the worker holds the Director-General's
-- written approval that he has no objection to the employment. 2 (¶13): the
-- approval is the Director-General's or a deputy's, and is a different thing
-- from the teaching licence the Ministry issues for post-primary education.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p12 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p13
DECLARE `approval action` IS ONE OF
    `employ an education worker` HAS `the worker holds the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `send the yearly circular to the owners and principals`
    `hand the application form to the candidate`
    `fill, sign and hand in the application form`
    `check, sign, stamp and forward the form to the personnel division`
    `carry out sample audits`
    `demand the worker's immediate dismissal`

DECLARE `who approves employment` IS ONE OF
    `the Director-General`
    `a deputy of the Director-General`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `given by` IS A `who approves employment`, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a valid employment approval` `given by` `in writing` IF
    `in writing` AND NOT `given by` EQUALS `someone else`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `approval action`
DECIDE `no employment without approval` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    SHANT `employ an education worker` a
          PROVIDED NOT a
    LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "Supervision of Schools Law, section 16A: no education worker is employed without the Director-General's approval"

-- 3 (¶14): every year, by the end of May, the personnel division sends the
-- owners a circular on the subject, with a copy straight to the principals.
-- Time in school months (September = 1).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p14
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `approval action`
DECIDE `the yearly circular` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `send the yearly circular to the owners and principals`
    WITHIN `month number` May
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "section 1.21.4(3): the circular goes out by the end of May"

-- 4–6 (¶15–¶18): the regulations of 1970 set an application form; the
-- principal gives it (original and copy) to every candidate; the worker
-- fills it, attaches the documents, signs and hands it to the principal; the
-- principal checks it, signs, stamps and sends it straight to the personnel
-- division by 30.11 of each year (school month 3).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p15 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p16 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p17 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p18
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `approval action`
DECIDE `the approval form's way` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `hand the application form to the candidate`
    HENCE (PARTY `the teaching employee`
           MUST  `fill, sign and hand in the application form`
           HENCE (PARTY `the school principal`
                  MUST  `check, sign, stamp and forward the form to the personnel division`
                  WITHIN `month number` November
                  LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.21.4(6)(ב): the form reaches the personnel division by 30.11"))

#TRACE `the approval form's way` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `hand the application form to the candidate` AT 1
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `fill, sign and hand in the application form` AT 1
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `check, sign, stamp and forward the form to the personnel division` AT 2

-- 7 (¶19): the Ministry carries out sample audits of this instruction.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p19
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `approval action`
DECIDE `sample audits` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `carry out sample audits`

-- 8 (¶20): where an education worker in an institution under the law has no
-- approval, the Director-General (or a deputy) may demand that the owner
-- dismiss him at once, even mid-year, and the Ministry neither budgets nor
-- reimburses the owner's salary costs that follow.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_21__ssec_1_21_3_11/p20
GIVEN `the worker holds the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `approval action`
DECIDE `dismissal without approval` `the worker holds the approval` IS
    IF `the worker holds the approval`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the director-general`
         MAY   `demand the worker's immediate dismissal`

GIVEN `the worker holds the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ministry funds the salary costs` `the worker holds the approval` IF
    `the worker holds the approval`

